# Line endings are NOT converted, ever.
#
# This repository deliberately holds both LF and CRLF files. The .ps1 scripts and some of the older
# Java sources were written by tools that chose CRLF; HANDOFF.zh-CN.md, patch/*.md and the newer Java
# files are LF. Nothing downstream cares -- javac, Gradle, PowerShell and the JSON parser all accept
# either -- but a conversion would: `core.autocrlf=true`, which the Git for Windows installer often
# sets, rewrites every LF file to CRLF on checkout, so the whole tree looks modified and real changes
# get buried in the noise. `-text` pins every file to exactly the bytes it has.
#
# Set per repository, not globally, so nothing else on this machine is affected.
* -text

# Binary: no diff attempted, and no conversion can ever happen to them.
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.gz binary
*.nbt binary
*.dat binary
